# L8-CTL (CONTROL): the strict ladder past 131k on eight pooled seats on the production audited profile and base image. Production went live with L8, C16, H1, H2 and P1 skipped, so this is the first card
# read of it. READ: concurrent byte-equal to solo for every user (the 140k and 253k rungs included), zero extent-audit mismatches, no refusal, no hang. A FAIL is a production finding (as P1b-CTL). Real time ~45.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production ENGINE: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's; production's thin layer on top of it is NOT exercised) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,32768,140000,253920,16384,65536,200000,253000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_GATE_AUDITS=extent
C2_GATE_SALT=fresh
